DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppddbbiimmggttooppaamm reads a Palm Pilot Image Viewer image (and Image record  in
       a  PDB  file) as input, from Standard Input or _p_a_l_m_f_i_l_e, and produces a
       PAM image as output.

       If the Pilot image is monochrome, the PAM output has maxval 1.   Other‐
       wise, it has maxval 255.  Note that Pilot images are always monochrome.
       The PAM image has tuple type GRAYSCALE.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  ), ppddbbiimmggttooppaamm recognizes
       the following command line options:



       --vveerrbboossee
              Display various interesting information about the input file and
              process.


       --nnootteeffiillee==_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
              Write the image note (if any) to the specified file.

              If you don't specify this, ppddbbiimmggttooppaamm ignores any image note.




